+Passing file descriptors
+------------------------
+
+Connections opened with `-passfds 1` keep file descriptors passed with
+SCM_RIGHTS instead of letting the kernel discard them when Tcl reads,
+and hand them out with `unix_sockets::fds` once the script has read the
+message they came with:
+
+~~~tcl
+set chan    [unix_sockets::connect /tmp/.foo -passfds 1]
+gets $chan line
+set files   [unix_sockets::fds $chan]
+~~~
+
+`unix_sockets::listen path accept -passfds 1` does the same for every
+accepted connection.  The default is unchanged.
+
